{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Three times a year you shall appear.</b> To give thanks for the freedom, and for the spring, and for the harvest, and for the ingathering — for from Him is everything." "<b>Before the Master.</b> The word 'master' may be said of one who directs affairs that would otherwise be subject to corruption. Accordingly, since He is the master of the people who appear before Him in particular, and when they appear before Him they are like a servant receiving his master's countenance — and He is also the master of the land, as it says (Leviticus 25:23): כִּי לִי הָאָרֶץ כִּי גֵרִים וְתוֹשָׁבִים אַתֶּם עִמָּדִי — therefore it is fitting to give thanks before Him for the spring, the harvest, and the ingathering, which are the produce of the land. And therefore."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:57.067605608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}